# @jamesjnadeau/content-tools is published to GitHub Packages, which requires
# a token even to install a public package. The token comes from the
# environment, never from this file: locally a classic PAT with read:packages,
# in GitHub Actions the job's GITHUB_TOKEN, on Netlify a NODE_AUTH_TOKEN
# environment variable set in the dashboard. Everything else still comes from
# registry.npmjs.org.
@jamesjnadeau:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}
